(7318232, 1141643, 174999, '<td valign="top">well done!!!!! Congrats on being in the top 30~!</td>', 'well done!!!!! Congrats on being in the top 30~!', '2015-02-18 08:16:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7318239, 1141685, 77196, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=177611" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">doodles</a> asked how I did that...<br/>First, I used a slow shutter speed (4/10 second), 100 ISO, and f/40 aperture - the goal being to keep the image from being overexposed. <br/>I also have a 16-300mm Tamron zoom lens, and I changed the zoom during the exposure. (So, shutter release, zoom in (or out), shutter closes). Sounds easier than it is, and this was one of about 15 attempts. You don''t have to have such an extreme range on the zoom to get the motion. This image happened to have a pause at each extreme, which is why the numbers seem to appear twice. <br/>Finally, in processing, I did a negative image on it - the scene was actually of a building number just below the roof - light background with red numbers.</td>', ' doodles asked how I did that...First, I used a slow shutter speed (4/10 second), 100 ISO, and f/40 aperture - the goal being to keep the image from being overexposed. I also have a 16-300mm Tamron zoom lens, and I changed the zoom during the exposure. (So, shutter release, zoom in (or out), shutter closes). Sounds easier than it is, and this was one of about 15 attempts. You don''t have to have such an extreme range on the zoom to get the motion. This image happened to have a pause at each extreme, which is why the numbers seem to appear twice. Finally, in processing, I did a negative image on it - the scene was actually of a building number just below the roof - light background with red numbers.', '2015-02-18 08:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7318242, 1141641, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damjanev:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by backdoorhippie:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damjanev:</b></div><hr/><i> If only there was 5318008 on the calculator display ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>What, 58008 wasn''t enough?! Boobies wouldn''t have fit in the composition.  ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The font was obscuring the message. It is not complete without calculator LCD typeface :-)<br/>Congrats on the Top10. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That was part of my intent and why I put it on the iPhone and not the calculator.  I''m a bit of a math nerd and much of the romance of the old calculation devises, including their ability to produce giggles from immature high school boys spelling things in the back of the room, has been lost with readable fonts and modern electronics.  So lost that even someone looking for it, as you were, couldn''t see it - and neither have any of the hundreds of viewers of this photo on various photo sharing sites.  <br/> <br/>:(<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-02-18 08:35:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by damjanev: Originally posted by backdoorhippie: Originally posted by damjanev: If only there was 5318008 on the calculator display ;-)   What, 58008 wasn''t enough?! Boobies wouldn''t have fit in the composition.  ;)   The font was obscuring the message. It is not complete without calculator LCD typeface :-)Congrats on the Top10.   That was part of my intent and why I put it on the iPhone and not the calculator.  I''m a bit of a math nerd and much of the romance of the old calculation devises, including their ability to produce giggles from immature high school boys spelling things in the back of the room, has been lost with readable fonts and modern electronics.  So lost that even someone looking for it, as you were, couldn''t see it - and neither have any of the hundreds of viewers of this photo on various photo sharing sites.   :(', '2015-02-18 08:35:06.000000', '2015-02-18 08:35:33.000000', 0),
