(7318503, 1141612, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyClick:</b></div><hr/><i> Lovely shot, Paul. Congratulations. But I''m curious what the "." represents?  Surely not the decimal place?! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Penny. not sure about the dot - possibly due to the farmer having so many sheep he has numbered one batch without dots and one with. I will ask the farmer next time I see him. Fortunately the field of sheep is in my village</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyClick: Lovely shot, Paul. Congratulations. But I''m curious what the "." represents?  Surely not the decimal place?!   Thanks Penny. not sure about the dot - possibly due to the farmer having so many sheep he has numbered one batch without dots and one with. I will ask the farmer next time I see him. Fortunately the field of sheep is in my village', '2015-02-18 23:16:14.000000', NULL, 0),
